toml`; put provider, notification, and telemetry keys in user-level config instead.\nL775: Config cite423†profile files live next to `config.toml` as `$CODEX_HOME/profile-name.config.toml`; select one with `--profile profile-name`.\nL776: For sandbox and approval keys (`approval_policy`, `sandbox_mode`, and `sandbox_workspace_write.*`), pair this reference with cite424†Sandbox and approvals , cite425†Protected paths in writable roots , and cite426†Network access . For beta permission profiles, see cite309†Permissions .\nL777: \nL778: [Input: Filter by key, type, or details]\nL779: Key  | Type / Values  | Details\nL780: --- | --- | ---\nL781: `agents`  | `table`  | Multi-agent settings and custom role declarations. Scalar setting names are reserved and can't be used as custom role names.\nL782: `agents.<name>.config_file`  | `string (path)`  | Path to a TOML config layer for that role; relative paths resolve from the config file that declares the role.\nL783: `agents.<name>.description`  | `string`  | Role guidance shown to Codex when choosing and spawning that agent type.\nL784: `agents.default_subagent_model`  | `string`  | Default model for spawned agents. An explicit spawn model takes precedence.\nL785: `agents.default_subagent_reasoning_effort`  | `string`  | Default reasoning effort for spawned agents. An explicit spawn effort takes precedence.\nL786: `agents.enabled`  | `boolean`  | Enable or disable multi-agent tools (default: true).\nL787: `agents.interrupt_message`  | `boolean`  | Record a model-visible message when an agent turn is interrupted (default: true).\nL788: `agents.max_concurrent_threads_per_session`  | `number`  | Maximum number of spawned-agent threads that can be open concurrently, excluding the primary thread. When unset, Codex chooses the default.\nL789: `agents.max_threads`  | `number`  | Legacy alias for `agents.max_concurrent_threads_per_session`.\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------